==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermittedRequiresAuthorization  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_PermittedRequiresAuthorization.als
    rationale: this fact carries every load-bearing condition tying a Permitted outcome to (a) role-allowance in the permission matrix and (b) the conditional care-team / ownership predicate. Clearing it lets the model invent a Permitted operation by a forbidden role/kind combination, which falsifies LeastPrivilege, OwnershipBasedAccess, and the contrapositive NoInformationLeakage assertion.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, OwnershipBasedAccess, NoInformationLeakage, FR_004_ClinicianCareTeamRequired, FR_006_PatientOwnRecordOnly, FR_007_ComplianceNoRecordRead, FR_008_ByteEquivalentForbidden
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_ClinicianCareTeamRequired: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_PatientOwnRecordOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ComplianceNoRecordRead: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_ByteEquivalentForbidden: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditPerOperation  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuditPerOperation.als
    rationale: this is the single fact enforcing the 1-to-1 correspondence between Operation and AuditEntry. Clearing it removes both the existence clause (every op has an AE) and the uniqueness clause (no two AEs share an op); injection forces an op with no AE, falsifying AuditCompleteness.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, AppendOnly, FR_013_AuditPerOp, FR_015_AuditImmutable
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_AuditPerOp: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttributionCorrect  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuditAttributionCorrect.als
    rationale: this fact forces each AuditEntry's snapshot fields (accessor, role, kind, outcome, ip, record, note) to equal the corresponding op's fields. Clearing it lets the model invent an AE whose accessor differs from its op's actor — direct misattribution.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_014_AuditFieldsComplete
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_AuditFieldsComplete: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NotesUniquelyCreated  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_NotesUniquelyCreated.als
    rationale: this fact says every ClinicalNote is referenced by exactly one creating operation. Clearing it lets two operations claim authorship of the same note, modelling the very mutation that the append-only invariant forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_012_NotesAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_NotesAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OperationTargetRules  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_OperationTargetRules.als
    rationale: this fact contains the 'opNote iff (PostNote and Permitted)' biconditional. Clearing it lets the model attach a created note to a Denied operation — exactly the validation-before-mutation violation (a side effect on a refused request).
    expected to FAIL: ValidationBeforeMutation
      - ValidationBeforeMutation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PatientHasAssignedRecord  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_PatientHasAssignedRecord.als
    rationale: this fact establishes the patient-record pairing iff. Clearing it lets the model invent a patient with no assigned record (orphan), violating OwnershipExclusivity.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipExclusivity, FR_003_PatientAssignedRecord
      - OwnershipExclusivity: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_003_PatientAssignedRecord: FAIL (expected)

